From 2f13a488416d9ed84c26cae5bf4642476a5b0816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:36:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] Colour range: Kodi's Auto, Full and Limited over
 CRgbRange

Kodi's b4fd1ce (smp79, Piers) replaces the boolean "Use limited colour
range (16-235)" on GBM with a "Colour range" setting of three values,
videoscreen.colorrange: Auto, Full (0-255) and Limited (16-235), sent to
the driver as the connector's "Broadcast RGB", with a one-time migration
of the boolean. Hades already drives "Broadcast RGB" for the limited range
(CRgbRange: the driver compresses once, a change waits for a mode set and
never comes while a video plays, refusals counted and given up, "Full" in
place of a refused "Limited 16:235", native Dolby Vision left alone).

This takes Kodi's setting, its ids, labels and migration, and keeps the
mechanics of Hades underneath instead of Kodi's own:
- CRgbRange works on a Choice (Auto, Full, Limited, the values of the
  setting) instead of a bool. Limited is the old setting on and Auto the
  old setting off, unchanged: only Kodi's own values are taken back to
  "Automatic". Full is new: "Full" is asked with a mode set of its own,
  Kodi draws full range, Auto takes Kodi's "Full" back, and after
  REFUSALS refused commits nothing more is asked.
- Native Dolby Vision is full range whatever the choice: its transport
  sets "Full" (TransportSpecs.h) and Stage() asks nothing while it holds
  the output; at its end the value found is put back as the choice of the
  moment asks (AtHandBack()).
- CRgbRange::Migrated(): the boolean on, with the colour range still at
  its default, becomes Limited; the boolean is turned off either way, so
  that Auto chosen later is not undone at the next start. The GBM window
  system shows the colour range and hides the boolean.
- The DRM PRIME renderer that cannot convert a format to limited range
  sets the colour range back to Auto as well, as in Kodi's commit.

Kodi's own ApplyBroadcastRange(), RetryBroadcastRange() and the setting
callback are not taken: Hades stages the property in FlipPage() with its
own retry and mode-set rules, which they would duplicate. Nor are the
per-frame range checks of Kodi's video renderers: in Hades who compresses
changes only with a mode set that the kernel took, and a per-frame check
would also follow native Dolby Vision's "Full" in the middle of a video.

Strings: Kodi's ids 36922 to 36925 in English, with a help text that says
what Hades does (Dolby Vision always full range, when a change applies);
Spanish (es_es, es_ar, es_mx) in Estuary 54922 to 54925, through
GetHadesString() as the other settings of Hades. "Auto" is Kodi's 16316.

Tests: TestRgbRange on the choice, plus Full asked, refused and taken
back, a Full that Kodi did not ask for left alone, Full chosen during a
video, the end of Dolby Vision with Full chosen, Dolby Vision full range
whatever the choice, and the migration.
